      "bullets": [
        "Explores dual-bootstrapping techniques between Forth's stack-based execution and Lisp's tree-structured evaluation models for embedded system runtimes.",
        "Leverages threaded code compilation and metacompilation to implement minimal, self-hosting interpreters without reliance on heavy standard libraries.",
        "Highlights architectural trade-offs between Forth's explicit parameter stacks and Lisp's dynamic memory allocation in micro-runtime design."
      ]
